1
00:00:01,060 --> 00:00:03,700
Come on, we're shining, running, forever!

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:06,740
The sea is calling out, so ride the waves!

3
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:09,557
We're all together as one,
so let's sail in the sun!

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:11,840
All our dreams are never-ending,

5
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:17,180
Heartbeat, we will be one! Go ahead!

6
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:26,557
Even though our hearts have
traveled different paths.

7
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,177
We are best friends.

8
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:30,037
Our freedom is our only compass.

9
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:34,197
That's pointing us along the
many roads that come together.

10
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,517
We will keep on running forward every day.

11
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,897
Go east, go west.

12
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:41,657
As long as we keep looking to the horizon.

13
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:44,360
We'll see everything all crystal clear.

14
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:50,340
We're all so thrilled that we
can't wait until the dawn arrives.

15
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:54,517
So we'll just bring the
sun ourselves to know.

16
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,740
If the winds blow, is waiting
where we should be going, go?

17
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:02,217
That's right, we're
shining, running forever.

18
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,257
All of our dreams will
merge into one piece.

19
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:07,977
No matter where we go,
we'll be fine and free.

20
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:10,354
Cause all our treasure is our strength.

21
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:13,297
Come on, we're shining, running forever.

22
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:16,137
The sea is coming out, so ride the wave.

23
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:17,537
We're all together as well.

24
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:19,017
So let's just stay with the sun.

25
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:21,337
While our dreams are never ending.

26
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,960
Heartbeat, we will be one, go ahead.

27
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:31,137
My darkness will swallow the world.

28
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:32,514
Just you wait and see.

29
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:35,000
You think I'll lose to you?

30
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:37,202
I'm gonna be king of the pirates

31
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,320
Roger's treasure belongs to me

32
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:47,617
We'll ride non-stop and travel farther

33
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:51,617
than we've ever gone And then tomorrow

34
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:57,760
we will find suspense And then commence
to live out another day so intense

35
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:00,187
That's right, we're shining,

36
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:05,237
running forever Let's go along
with curiosity Our feelings lead

37
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:10,940
the way straight to a brand new day Into
another adventure Come on, we're shining,

38
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:16,720
running forever Open the map inside your
heart and see No matter where we end up,

39
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:22,220
our mods will never give up There's a fire
in our dreams and you can never, never,

40
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:25,840
never, never stop it We
will be one, go ahead!

41
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,997
This rock guy doesn't want
to let us go anywhere.

42
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:52,100
Like I told you, Fika
controls the entire palace.

43
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:54,616
We're lucky he hasn't crushed us yet.

44
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,000
Hey, Straw Hat.

45
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:03,860
You're sure your friend will
be okay? Zoro? Are you kidding?

46
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:06,220
He'll do great. Don't worry.

47
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,285
No matter what happens,
Zoro will pull through.

48
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,960
What's the trick here?

49
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:25,181
There has to be some place that can cut
this bastard that'll take him down for good.

50
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:30,180
That's not good!

51
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,127
We've got another executive!

52
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:36,180
He's a member of the Pika Army.

53
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,030
Gladius!

54
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:40,497
You can't beat him in your current form.

55
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:43,756
Rampo and I will draw his
attention and you run ahead!

56
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:45,236
That's the only way!

57
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,282
Don't you dare!

58
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:50,120
I won't have you sacrifice
yourselves on my behalf! Rampo!

59
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:53,360
We'll attack from both
sides at once! Roger!

60
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:55,770
No way!

61
00:03:57,620 --> 00:04:00,840
Can't believe I'm stuck
exterminating these rats!

62
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,340
Let them go!

63
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:37,000
You think a toy can outrun me.

64
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:47,000
I ate the pop-pop fruit
and became a rupture man.

65
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:54,160
That means I can detonate my body
without causing harm to myself.

66
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:55,900
But that's not all.

67
00:04:57,960 --> 00:05:01,600
I can also detonate anything inorganic.

68
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:06,300
Though a toy like you
won't survive the process.

69
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,540
Don't you dare.

70
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,160
I refuse to die.

71
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,300
Someone is counting on me!

72
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:20,650
Rebecca!

73
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:24,720
Looks like you're ready
to burst, little toy!

74
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,560
Jack, stop!

75
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,680
Who did that?

76
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:40,160
Soldier, have you seen my crew?

77
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:41,740
You saved me.

78
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,157
Freaky made it sound like he was with you.

79
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,077
There's no time.

80
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,737
You can talk later, Starhat.

81
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,260
So that's who it is.

82
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,390
Violet!

83
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:52,640
You little traitor.

84
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:57,400
You'll pay for turning your
back on the young master.

85
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,177
Oh, you want to fight?

86
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,120
What did I just say? Let go!

87
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:04,060
We have to run. Trust me. He's strong.

88
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,377
We'd be trapped here.

89
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:06,636
We have to end this.

90
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,257
Just head for the suit chamber.

91
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:10,360
Lady Viola, you're helping us now?

92
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:13,440
You recognize me? Of course!

93
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:16,177
Although I'm sure that
you've forgotten me.

94
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:17,117
That may be so.

95
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:20,237
But I've been watching you with my
clairvoyance for quite some time.

96
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:22,140
You and Rebecca as well. What?

97
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:24,060
I know it's been hard.

98
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:25,380
So thank you.

99
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:27,260
Get back here!

100
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:32,200
Your treachery won't
go unpunished, Violet.

101
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,520
You're dead!

102
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,977
I've never been on your side!

103
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:40,180
You give yourself too much credit.

104
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:43,297
For ten whole years, I've been
waiting for this opportunity!

105
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:46,760
I won't hear your
venomous words any longer.

106
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:48,620
Helmet, pop!

107
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,840
Lady Viola! Oh, no!

108
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,777
Sorry, I should've caught that.

109
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:03,457
Didn't get hurt too bad, did you?

110
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:05,237
Doesn't matter how we get there, right?

111
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,197
Where are you going?

112
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,104
The staircase is the other way!

113
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:14,400
This is bad.

114
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:15,537
What are you doing?

115
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,620
That should work.

116
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,300
Where did they go?

117
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:31,580
Young Master, why are you here?

118
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:35,877
Young Master?

119
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:38,607
The Doflamingo family
calls him young master.

120
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:40,720
That would be me.

121
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:44,197
There are some intruders in the palace.

122
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:47,357
You might want to wait upstairs
until we take care of them.

123
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:48,270
Upstairs?

124
00:07:48,353 --> 00:07:49,431
I shall do no such thing.

125
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:53,237
You may do as you wish with the
intruders, but I'm heading underground.

126
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,180
I have business with Kanjido.

127
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:58,546
The samurai who disappeared
from the junkyard?

128
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,250
Huh?

129
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,127
Did you say he went missing?

130
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:05,637
Well, that certainly was
effective, wasn't it?

131
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,550
It's not time yet.

132
00:08:06,633 --> 00:08:08,057
You have to wait first.

133
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:09,677
We have to hurry, and now we have to wait.

134
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,097
Mingo is right. There!

135
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:13,477
Just calm down.

136
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,897
The Tontara still need time to finish.

137
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:21,397
I thought your only objective

138
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,357
was to destroy the Smile Factory.

139
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,397
So what about Straw Hat?

140
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:28,437
His crew is teaming up
with the little people

141
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,797
from Green Bit—would
you mind telling me why?

142
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:33,617
Even for them, that
seems a bit capricious.

143
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:34,777
Doesn't it?

144
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:40,017
Little people—while you're at it—tell me
how they snuck into the underground port.

145
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:41,080
But why did

146
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:47,677
they decide to target Sugar?

147
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:52,517
I can't figure out their motivations
or how they arrived at this plan.

148
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:56,597
But they're doing a good job of
pissing me off at this point.

149
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:59,580
It's looking like... it's looking like

150
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:05,157
more than a simple coincidence.

151
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,317
That's not good.

152
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:10,520
Because that would mean they know
about this kingdom's dark secrets.

153
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:17,100
Don't just sit there!

154
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:19,633
The young master's speaking to you, Law!

155
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:26,214
Don't do it if it's gonna make you cry!

156
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:28,800
I swear, you two never change!

157
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:32,177
I already told you.

158
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:34,966
I don't have anything
to do with them anymore.

159
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:36,777
Our alliance ended.

160
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:40,331
Whatever they're doing out
there, it's none of my business.

161
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:53,380
A pity Violet isn't here.

162
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:55,737
She could see right through
you if you were lying.

163
00:09:55,820 --> 00:10:01,200
By the way, you wouldn't happen to know
anything about this, would you, King Rick?

164
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:05,680
The Tontada were rather
fond of you, if I recall.

165
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:09,990
Father?

166
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:11,420
Why is he here?

167
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:14,120
Traffy's okay. That's good.

168
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:19,280
King Rick, after all these
years, you're still alive.

169
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,560
Your name is Kiros, huh?

170
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,919
Why don't you come with me, friend?

171
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:27,720
I will save you.

172
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,200
I swear it.

173
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,317
Let's go kick Mingo's ass already.

174
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,517
We still have to wait for the Tontara.

175
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,247
Did something happen to Leo?

176
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,597
Our window for victory is narrow,

177
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:40,597
but as long as he can restore
the toys to their human form,

178
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:44,386
I'll have my chance to strike
down Doflamingo once and for all.

179
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:48,197
My friends put their lives
on the line to protect me.

180
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:50,480
I will not fail, no matter the cost.

181
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,520
I'm counting on you, Leo.

182
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:54,170
Usoland!

183
00:10:58,220 --> 00:11:01,985
Just give yourself up, Franky,
or we'll fire until you're dead!

184
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,500
You kidding me?

185
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:06,460
Why don't you shut the hell up?

186
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:12,820
Listen up, losers.

187
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:16,177
I'm going to go nuts and
wreck this place all day long.

188
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:18,160
Don't ask me why. What?

189
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,937
If I go underground with
these chumps chasing me,

190
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:26,897
It's just gonna make
things worse for the little

191
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:31,157
people I'm leaving operation
SOP in your hands, bros.

192
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:33,780
Give me everything you got.

193
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:37,857
Do your thing!

194
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:38,770
Who's a wind?

195
00:11:38,853 --> 00:11:39,960
I got your back!

196
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:43,431
Whoa, what the hell's going on over there?

197
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:47,797
They said we've got intruders
We've also got master trebles and

198
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:51,497
no big deal those poor bastards
once you get on his bad side,

199
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:53,168
then you're as good as dead

200
00:11:58,640 --> 00:12:00,640
What'd you guys take down already?

201
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,020
Jeez, you wanna die?

202
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,720
I dropped my guard.

203
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,700
I've been turned into a toy.

204
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,329
That means everyone
has forgotten about me.

205
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:16,770
Who's up?

206
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:18,460
Where did you go?

207
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,741
There's nothing I can do anymore.

208
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:23,740
It's all up to you now.

209
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:26,969
Whatever it takes, you
have to fight a way.

210
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:28,960
It's funny.

211
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:32,515
Why were they trying so hard
to make me eat this grape?

212
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:35,020
Probably poison, huh?

213
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:37,520
It certainly smells terrible.

214
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,100
I can't do it.

215
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,880
I can't fight anymore.

216
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:43,441
And don't worry.

217
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:46,893
If anything goes wrong, I'll
jump in and take over, okay?

218
00:12:48,380 --> 00:12:49,210
Usoland.

219
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:52,440
Move! What happened? Come back!

220
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:59,000
I'm sorry, but I want to live. Who's up?

221
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:00,220
Where did you go?

222
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:02,460
We need you. Oh, hey.

223
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:06,697
How about I write a book to tell
future generations how brave you are?

224
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:08,080
The Honest Tantadas.

225
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,720
I've got a name already.

226
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:12,080
Good thing I'm alive, huh?

227
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:14,317
All of this is Frankie's fault anyway.

228
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,282
Why didn't he come here to help?

229
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:21,137
I won't let myself get killed just because
you guys think I'm some legendary hero.

230
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:23,420
Okay, I got away from the bad guys.

231
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:27,034
But I still need to find a
way out of this stupid place.

232
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:31,977
Probably can't worm my way through the
tunnel without them carrying me, huh?

233
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:32,940
Oh, wait.

234
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:35,217
They said that there
was a lift, didn't they?

235
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:37,580
Hey, hey, can everybody hear me?

236
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,640
Is it a show?

237
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:42,215
I hope you're not just standing there.

238
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:44,381
You didn't stop working, did you?

239
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,240
Ah, crap.

240
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:48,140
Get back to work.

241
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,360
Move those boxes.

242
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,608
What are you doing, stupid?

243
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:55,080
Hurry up, or else!

244
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:58,284
Someone's standing up to
the Don Quixote family!

245
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:02,540
I've been a toy for eight years and
I haven't seen this happen once!

246
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:05,020
Whoever you are, good luck!

247
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:06,560
Burn it all down!

248
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:08,760
Standing around?

249
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,294
I'm getting the hell out of this place!

250
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:14,119
What should we do with all of them?

251
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,360
Hmm... Huh?

252
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:18,110
Sugar?

253
00:14:18,193 --> 00:14:20,200
Hey, are they saying something?

254
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:22,180
Sounds like it's... Huh? Huh?

255
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,080
U...

256
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,097
So...

257
00:14:26,180 --> 00:14:27,060
Lund.

258
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:28,910
U...

259
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,000
So...

260
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:32,820
Uso... Lund.

261
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:35,940
Uso...

262
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:37,910
Uso...

263
00:14:37,993 --> 00:14:39,340
Lund, please.

264
